00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:48.740
in town,

00:11:49.515 --> 00:11:50.235
And

00:11:50.795 --> 00:11:51.435
we

00:11:51.915 --> 00:11:53.515
we we spent

00:11:54.075 --> 00:11:57.675
quite quite a bit of time actually looking at several locations,

00:12:00.315 --> 00:12:00.955
and

00:12:01.770 --> 00:12:08.490
there were some different recommendations. So I don't know if tonight's focus is specifically those roads around the lake area,

00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:14.730
but we did look at some other locations, but I think tonight is focusing on on the lake area, if I'm correct. You are correct.

00:12:15.335 --> 00:12:16.455
Okay. So,

00:12:17.575 --> 00:12:18.455
you know,

00:12:19.175 --> 00:12:22.375
based on my conversation with Eric and certainly,

00:12:23.255 --> 00:12:23.895
you know,

00:12:24.775 --> 00:12:26.055
tonight's discussion,

00:12:26.855 --> 00:12:31.570
I can answer any questions that come up or or we can talk about other options. But

00:12:32.290 --> 00:12:33.170
initially,

00:12:33.890 --> 00:12:39.570
what Eric and I discussed was the fact that, you know, this is a a busy area,

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:42.290
a seasonally busy area,

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:44.290
and that

00:12:44.485 --> 00:12:48.165
there are concerns with speeds through the area.

00:12:49.205 --> 00:12:50.325
You know, obviously,

00:12:50.485 --> 00:12:53.205
even the day that we were there, which was in late May,

00:12:53.365 --> 00:12:56.405
there were already people walking and biking.

00:12:57.790 --> 00:13:01.710
Know, Eric said that only was going to increase with the summertime.

00:13:04.750 --> 00:13:05.390
So,

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:07.390
you know, there

00:13:09.150 --> 00:13:10.670
were certain things that I noticed

00:13:11.235 --> 00:13:13.555
as we walked around and drove around.

00:13:13.795 --> 00:13:16.435
One of the things that I recommended,

00:13:16.835 --> 00:13:20.595
and there was some talk and I know Eric shared some notes that he had made,

00:13:21.955 --> 00:13:24.035
but you know, regarding striping,

00:13:24.035 --> 00:13:24.275
so

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:32.500
well, first and foremost, if you do centerline striping, has to be a double yellow line, not a single yellow line.

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:34.820
But

00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:36.740
often

00:13:36.820 --> 00:13:41.565
I recommend to towns that have streets like the ones in that area,

00:13:42.605 --> 00:13:45.885
no centerline striping and edgeline striping only.

00:13:47.485 --> 00:13:51.885
That is allowed per the federal manual. There are some requirements,

00:13:53.085 --> 00:13:57.680
but the roads in question that I recommended it for meet those requirements.

00:13:59.760 --> 00:14:00.640
The

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:03.120
point of that is that

00:14:04.080 --> 00:14:05.040
psychologically,

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:08.865
see a double yellow line and they think main road,

00:14:09.105 --> 00:14:10.545
they think high speed.

00:14:11.265 --> 00:14:17.505
When you remove that and you just put the edge line striping in and you narrow the travel lanes and you

00:14:18.785 --> 00:14:21.585
make people have to think about where to drive,

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:25.090
They're avoiding that edge line striping,

00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:28.050
but they know there could be cars coming in the other direction,

00:14:28.370 --> 00:14:34.210
so they tend to drive a little bit slower, bring their speeds down because they have to be more cautious.

00:14:35.835 --> 00:14:42.555
And then the added benefit of an edge line stripe is that it gives pedestrians and cyclists a spot to stay on the shoulder.

00:14:43.195 --> 00:14:43.755
So

00:14:44.155 --> 00:14:45.835
we talked about some of that.

00:14:46.795 --> 00:14:49.115
There were a few other spots

00:14:49.115 --> 00:14:49.355
where

00:14:51.140 --> 00:14:56.420
there was an intersection, and you'll have to forgive me, I don't remember the name of the roads we were at,

