00:17:56.275 --> 00:17:57.715
How does chicanes

00:17:57.715 --> 00:17:58.755
work exactly?

00:18:00.275 --> 00:18:01.315
>> So

00:18:01.315 --> 00:18:02.755
chicanes basically

00:18:02.755 --> 00:18:03.395
are,

00:18:04.435 --> 00:18:05.315
if you imagine,

00:18:06.195 --> 00:18:08.675
we call them like a serpentine

00:18:08.450 --> 00:18:09.330
design.

00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:10.210
So

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:13.010
what a chicane does is it bumps out,

00:18:13.890 --> 00:18:20.610
think of like a curb bump out, but this is in the middle of the block and it's a longer narrower

00:18:20.850 --> 00:18:21.650
extension

00:18:21.785 --> 00:18:24.505
so that as you drive down the street,

00:18:26.985 --> 00:18:31.785
you drive out and around and back into it. So the lane

00:18:32.985 --> 00:18:34.985
kind of serpentines around

00:18:34.985 --> 00:18:38.040
these extensions and you offset them

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:42.040
so that as people come, they have to slow down

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:45.560
to go around as the two way traffic. I mean, it's almost,

00:18:45.800 --> 00:18:50.040
you know, if you imagine like a work zone where they have the lane shift,

00:18:51.535 --> 00:18:54.655
it works very similar to that, but it's it's,

00:18:55.375 --> 00:19:00.655
you know, offset so that each direction is doing it at a different point in the road.

00:19:01.135 --> 00:19:02.015
Does

00:19:02.095 --> 00:19:06.750
>> that make sense? I explain that okay? Is it is this done with, like, concrete barriers, or how is this done?

00:19:07.470 --> 00:19:10.670
>> So a a permanent installation is normally

00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:13.630
done with curbing,

00:19:13.870 --> 00:19:17.055
and, you know, you would most likely landscape it.

00:19:17.295 --> 00:19:17.695
There

00:19:19.135 --> 00:19:23.055
are some versions that are done with just paint.

00:19:23.935 --> 00:19:27.455
