00:20:15.335 --> 00:20:18.215
Speed is definitely an issue on these

00:20:18.695 --> 00:20:20.135
lake road areas specifically.

00:20:22.760 --> 00:20:24.360
>> Speed humps are

00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:26.360
traffic calming tool.

00:20:27.480 --> 00:20:31.240
You would want humps, not bumps. Bumps are like the really

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:32.280
small

00:20:32.440 --> 00:20:36.840
and severe ones that they put in parking lots that you have to go about five miles per hour

00:20:36.875 --> 00:20:40.315
drive over so you don't damage your car, but on public roads

00:20:40.635 --> 00:20:43.115
it would be a hump, so it would be a longer,

00:20:43.915 --> 00:20:44.875
less severe

00:20:46.075 --> 00:20:47.435
rise in the hump,

00:20:47.995 --> 00:20:48.315
and

00:20:49.370 --> 00:20:54.970
there are a lot of towns that have them, they definitely are a tool in the toolbox.

00:20:54.970 --> 00:20:56.090
I will say that,

00:20:57.610 --> 00:20:58.650
you know, they

00:20:59.050 --> 00:21:01.930
have what I would consider equal pros and cons.

00:21:04.015 --> 00:21:09.455
They do slow traffic, but they tend to only slow traffic right at that location.

00:21:09.775 --> 00:21:10.815
And then people

00:21:11.935 --> 00:21:15.695
like to speed up afterwards to make up for the time they had to slow down to go over it.

00:21:17.880 --> 00:21:18.920
I've also,

00:21:19.160 --> 00:21:22.760
you know, heard stories and seen examples of people

00:21:23.320 --> 00:21:24.280
driving

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:29.320
on the side of the road and on people's lawns, so they try to go around them.

00:21:32.015 --> 00:21:40.255
I've heard residents complain about noise when their house was the one that the hump was in front of. I mean, are pros and cons to them, so you'd have to really

00:21:40.495 --> 00:21:42.095
look at your locations.

00:21:42.095 --> 00:21:53.630
The other thing about humps is that they really only are effective if you have a series of them, so you'd have to look at the roadway and see, they have to be spaced out a certain amount of distance apart from one another,

00:21:54.350 --> 00:21:55.710
they can't be on

00:21:56.030 --> 00:21:57.150
curves or

00:21:57.895 --> 00:22:02.535
grade and you have to consider where driveways are, and then you have to consider drainage.

00:22:02.775 --> 00:22:03.815
So I mean,

00:22:04.375 --> 00:22:08.855
they are absolutely an option and I recommend them sometimes when I think that they're appropriate.

00:22:10.560 --> 00:22:14.160
